WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.933
Use BUILD: baseline, use AI, inspect, lead, and

00:00:05.991 --> 00:00:09.462
demonstrate. In this fictional tabletop, the baseline says

00:00:09.996 --> 00:00:13.247
complete intake can move directly to delivery. The

00:00:13.293 --> 00:00:16.718
human review identifies a defect: input completeness does

00:00:16.765 --> 00:00:19.365
not mean the output is approved. AI helps

00:00:19.412 --> 00:00:21.362
draft a correction, and the person checks it

00:00:21.397 --> 00:00:24.538
against the charter. The revised process keeps an

00:00:24.596 --> 00:00:27.475
incomplete intake pending, sends a complete draft to

00:00:27.545 --> 00:00:30.343
the named reviewer, and requires recorded human approval

00:00:30.401 --> 00:00:33.315
before delivery. A missing date remains a question.

00:00:33.768 --> 00:00:37.564
Preserve the useful request, output, version, and decision.

00:00:38.214 --> 00:00:40.931
The correction is material because it changes behavior

00:00:40.989 --> 00:00:42.998
required by the charter. It is still a

00:00:43.056 --> 00:00:47.151
tabletop design. It establishes no live integration or

00:00:47.221 --> 00:00:50.437
sending permission. Explain the defect, the decision, and

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:51.923
the behavior you will retest.
